{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Because. The Shiloah.</b> Some say they are Jerusalem. The correct view is the kingdom of the House of David, since most of the kings of the House of David were righteous, while all the kings of Israel were evil and sinful. The meaning of Shiloah is like flowing waters, or waters that a person sends forth, or waters that produce shoots, as in 'your shoots [שלחיך] are an orchard of pomegranates' (Song of Songs 4:13)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:48.520367452Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}